cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use karml, please cite it as below (and the associated paper once published)."
title: "karml: machine-learned potentials in molecular-mechanics MD"
# TODO(author): confirm the title, the full author list and order, and ORCID iDs before the first release.
authors:
  - family-names: Boittier
    given-names: Eric
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # TODO(author)
  # TODO(author): add co-authors of the software here (the manuscript authors are not assumed to be software authors).
repository-code: "https://github.com/EricBoittier/karml"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  karml (pronounced Karamell) combines CHARMM MLpot and JAX-MD with JAX-based neural models (PhysNet, DCMNet and others)
  for hybrid ML/MM condensed-phase simulations.
keywords:
  - molecular dynamics
  - machine-learned potentials
  - ML/MM
  - JAX
